Interpretation and limits:
  - A and B prove counted live /init nonce echo on two independent single-run series and their comparator has no unexplained differences.
  - C exercises the required common-ID two-run manifest, but aggregate failed because run 1 failed. Run 2 does not erase that result.
  - Independent triage: firmware_board.rs maps any IrqDeliveryFailure::Refused(_) to a generic error. The captured C/1 evidence lacks vector, detailed refusal, CPL/RIP and stop/UART state, so the exact cause is undetermined. It is consistent with the unverified S4-39h external-IRQ-from-CPL3 boundary, but does not prove that cause. ISSUE-088 (syscall journal queue counters) is unrelated.
  - The comparator compares two series by matching runs at the same index; the series writer aggregates statuses and validates unique nonces but does not compare runs within one series.
  - These are runner-recorded stop-scoped COM1 captures, not independent streaming UART traces. S5-06 A-G were not booted or executed as guest scenarios. S5-07 and Stage 5 remain unaccepted.
